From 1d19eef9a2004f5989473b94ec6c2919fc41cafd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:08:43 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ci(gate): batch lanes for separate runners (--lane N/M)
 and gate-verdict

`cargo xtask gate batch --lane N/M` runs lane N of M of the batch plan.
The split is a round-robin deal in plan order and reads no timing file,
so each runner computes the same lanes. Each test step and clippy is in
exactly one lane; a lane builds only the crates that it tests. A lane
run writes lane-result.tsv into its gate-logs dir.

`cargo xtask gate-verdict <dir>...` reads the records of all lanes and
prints one verdict: each lane with its runner, time and result, and the
red steps by name. A lane with no record, two records, a void run or
fewer steps than its plan makes the verdict red.

The workflow (post-merge.yml) does not use the lanes yet.

Refs #2908

